System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: &quot;Fluvial landforms&quot; are features on the Earth&apos;s surface produced by the action, i.e. erosion and deposition, of a stream or river and include such landforms as bars, levees, braided and meandering channels, and alluvial fans.  &quot;Fluvial processes&quot; are those processes included in the action of running water in a stream or river
