    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">&apos;Fluvial landforms&apos; are features on the Earth&apos;s surface produced by the action, i.e. erosion and deposition, of a stream or river and include such landforms as bars, levees, braided and meandering channels, and alluvial fans.  &apos;Fluvial processes&apos; are those processes included in the action of running water in a stream or river</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-10-04 09:43:22.0</dcterms:modified>
