    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-10-03 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Coastal processes refers to the action of natural forces (e.g. erosion,
deposition, tectonic uplift) on the shoreline, and the nearshore seabed.  Some
examples of landforms resulting from these processes are wave-cut cliffs,
beaches, and wave-cut benches.
New Value=Coastal processes refers to the action of natural forces (e.g. erosion,
deposition, tectonic uplift) on the shoreline, and the nearshore seabed.  Some
examples of landforms resulting from these processes are wave-cut cliffs,
beaches, and wave-cut benches.</skos:changeNote>
