    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Coastal processes refers to the action of natural forces (e.g. erosion,deposition, tectonic uplift) on the shoreline, and the nearshore seabed.  Someexamples of landforms resulting from these processes are wave-cut cliffs,beaches, and wave-cut benches.</skos:definition>
