    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Caltech Submillimeter Observatory" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The rate and speed at which the Earth rotates around its own axis. The Earth rotates towards the east. As viewed from the North Star Polaris, the Earth turns counter-clockwise.</skos:definition>
