  <skos:Concept rdf:about="bbfe00ab-ab63-40e0-8752-8f47d17c1d39">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="05172a3b-cdc0-4e97-af29-e38cd4f271c6"/>
    <dcterms:created>2013-03-05</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SUBSURFACE DRAINAGE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-04-01 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Refers to the removal of surface water by development of the slope of the land utilizing systems of drains to carry away the surplus water. In subsurface drainage open ditches and tile fields intercept groundwater and carry it off. The water enters the tiling through the joints, and drainage is achieved by gravity feed through the tiles.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-05 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=SUBSURFACE DRAINAGE [bbfe00ab-ab63-40e0-8752-8f47d17c1d39,82883] - KARST HYDROLOGY [05172a3b-cdc0-4e97-af29-e38cd4f271c6,82881]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Refers to the removal of surface water by development of the slope of the land utilizing systems of drains to carry away the surplus water. In subsurface drainage open ditches and tile fields intercept groundwater and carry it off. The water enters the tiling through the joints, and drainage is achieved by gravity feed through the tiles.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-04-01 14:03:41.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="f7998303-d145-452d-bcff-770f62038909">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="048df94e-841d-4f4d-a5c5-6683d1d07aa6"/>
    <dcterms:created>2013-02-18</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ISOTOPE RATIOS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-02-18 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ISOTOPE RATIOS [f7998303-d145-452d-bcff-770f62038909,82365] - GEOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES [048df94e-841d-4f4d-a5c5-6683d1d07aa6,82357]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The identification of isotopic signature, the distribution of certain stable isotopes and chemical elements within chemical compounds. This can be applied to a food web to make it possible to draw direct inferences regarding diet, trophic level, and subsistence. Isotope ratios are measured using mass spectrometry, which separates the different isotopes of an element on the basis of their mass-to-charge ratio.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="National Academy of Sciences" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The identification of isotopic signature, the distribution of certain stable isotopes and chemical elements within chemical compounds. This can be applied to a food web to make it possible to draw direct inferences regarding diet, trophic level, and subsistence. Isotope ratios are measured using mass spectrometry, which separates the different isotopes of an element on the basis of their mass-to-charge ratio.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-03-11 13:35:47.0</dcterms:modified>
