System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The standard measure of a tropical cyclone&apos;s intensity. When the term is applied to a particular weather system, it refers to the highest one-minute average wind (at an elevation of 10 meters with an unobstructed exposure) associated with that weather system at a particular point in time.
