    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="dd54dfac-069b-4552-abfe-d182320189c7"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The standard measure of a tropical cyclone&apos;s intensity. When the term is applied to a particular weather system, it refers to the highest one-minute average wind (at an elevation of 10 meters with an unobstructed exposure) associated with that weather system at a particular point in time.</skos:definition>
