    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="b016722f-5441-41c1-97c4-6612c87c4311"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The acoustic energy above which a single desired signal is heard. Inthe oceans, ambient noise can be produced physically (e.g. wind, rain,bubbles) or biologically (e.g. whales, dolphins).</skos:definition>
