    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Weather and Climate, American Meteorological Society, 1996." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A freezing precipitation form where rain that falls in liquid formbecomes supercooled and freezes upon impact with cold surfaces (atsubfreezing temperatures) to form a coating of glaze upon the ground andexposed objects.</skos:definition>
