example carbon exists in three isotopes: C12, C13, and C14. Some isotopes are
naturally unstable and spontaneously decay at a fixed rate; other isotopes are
stable.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Ice Age Terms. &apos;http://academic.emporia.edu/aberjame/ice/gloss.htm&apos;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Isotopes are a form of an element with a certain number of neutrons, forexample carbon exists in three isotopes: C12, C13, and C14. Some isotopes arenaturally unstable and spontaneously decay at a fixed rate; other isotopes arestable.</skos:definition>
