  <skos:Concept rdf:about="9efbc088-ba8c-4c9c-a458-ad6ad63f4188">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="08fd82a1-4370-46a2-82ea-94c0f91498a7"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ATMOSPHERIC PRESSURE MEASUREMENTS</skos:prefLabel>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Weather and Climate, American Meteorological Society, 1996.  &lt;B&gt;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The force exerted per unit of area by the atmosphere as a consequenceof gravitational attraction upon the &apos;column&apos; of air lying directly abovethe point in question.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="a2987914-ed66-4b7c-964d-8eccf0174e57">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="08a4f002-f368-414d-b923-83dd498452d8"/>
    <dcterms:created>2012-06-26</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ELECTRICAL PROPERTIES</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=gee-cee Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ELECTRICAL PROPERTIES [a2987914-ed66-4b7c-964d-8eccf0174e57,40133] - ICE CORE RECORDS [08a4f002-f368-414d-b923-83dd498452d8,40095]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-23 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: An important baseline measurement in ice cores is electrical conductivity. Electrical conductivity measurements (ECM) of the core is a very rapid method to indicate how acidic the core is without the chemical detail of the ion analyses. The value of the measurement is that it can be done for the whole length of the core in high resolution and provide an immediate picture of the core and allow quick detection of interesting areas, such as a volcanic eruptions. Because it is a high resolution, continuous measurement it can be used, along with the other measurements, for time frequency analysis in order to identify cycles in the climate signal.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="GISP2 (Greenland) Ice Cores and Climate Change: http://www.gisp2.sr.unh.edu/GISP2/MoreInfo/Ice_Cores_Past.html" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An important baseline measurement in ice cores is electrical conductivity. Electrical conductivity measurements (ECM) of the core is a very rapid method to indicate how acidic the core is without the chemical detail of the ion analyses. The value of the measurement is that it can be done for the whole length of the core in high resolution and provide an immediate picture of the core and allow quick detection of interesting areas, such as a volcanic eruptions. Because it is a high resolution, continuous measurement it can be used, along with the other measurements, for time frequency analysis in order to identify cycles in the climate signal.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-07-23 15:30:29.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
