    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from: Neshyba, S.  1987.  Oceanography, Perspectives on a Fluid Earth. John Wiley &amp; Sons, Inc. p. 489." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A rise above normal sea level on the coast where the Ekman effect, fromstrong winds, causes the shallow waters to pile up against the shore.</skos:definition>
