    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Coastal processes refers to the action of natural forces (e.g., erosion, deposition, tectonic uplift) on the shoreline, and the nearshore seabed. Some examples of landforms resulting from these processes arewave-cut cliffs, beaches, and wave-cut benches.</skos:definition>
