  <skos:Concept rdf:about="a81f6b17-2a16-4600-84b6-bcbcc5c29d2f">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="18d9ddbb-66cc-4b92-aa8d-2395ab3a17ce"/>
    <dcterms:created>2021-02-26</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ATMOSPHERIC RADON</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-03-04 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Radon is a chemical element with the symbol Rn and atomic number 86. It is a radioactive, colorless, odorless, tasteless noble gas. It occurs naturally in minute quantities as an intermediate step in the normal radioactive decay chains through which thorium and uranium slowly decay into lead and various other short-lived radioactive elements. Radon itself is the immediate decay product of radium.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-02-26 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
