    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">GLACIER/ICE CAVES</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-04-01 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Refers to any type of natural cave (most commonly lava tubes or limestone caves) that contains significant amounts of perennial (year-round) ice. At least a portion of the cave must have a temperature below 0 °C (32 °F) all year round, and water must have traveled into the cave’s cold zone.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
