    <skos:changeNote>Date=2016-06-13 User Id=gee-cee Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add narrower relation
New Value=SHRUBLAND/SCRUB [e018b139-7e05-4155-8e2e-8d5603b5fe47,84663] - MONTANE SHRUBLAND [9409e1f9-f3a9-46fa-aaf9-0e685ca2adcb,188189]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="The Nature Conservancy" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="0cc6527e-d162-4951-9db7-a6afe5c631c0"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="9409e1f9-f3a9-46fa-aaf9-0e685ca2adcb"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Areas with vegetation dominated by shrubs (generally greater than 0.5 m or 1.5 ft tall, but less than 5 m or 16 ft tall) with individuals or clumps overlapping to not touching (generally forming more  than 25%cover, trees generally less than 25% cover).</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2016-06-15 09:05:18.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="b40d8d03-6286-48cd-818c-20d1680d6453">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="09d1435d-99de-4149-ba64-d98c3335a383"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">CORONAL MASS EJECTION</skos:prefLabel>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Space Studies Board, Commission on Physical Sciences, Mathematics, and Applications National Research Council &apos;http://www.nas.edu/ssb/glossary.html&apos;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A disturbance of the Sun&apos;s corona involving eruptions from the lower part ofthe corona and ejection of large quantities of matter into the solar wind.These ejecta sometimes have higher speed, density, and magnetic field strengththan is typical for the solar wind. If their speeds relative to the backgroundsolar wind are high, they can produce shocks in the plasma that precede them asthey move outward.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="fa47cab9-0aa4-4e16-8115-972f7f543920">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="0c279e58-9ad3-4748-816a-de8cabeaf0c4"/>
    <dcterms:created>2013-02-18</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">CRESCENTIC (BARCHAN/TRANSVERSE) DUNE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-02-18 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=CRESCENTIC (BARCHAN/TRANSVERSE) DUNE [fa47cab9-0aa4-4e16-8115-972f7f543920,82583] - DUNES [0c279e58-9ad3-4748-816a-de8cabeaf0c4,82581]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-29 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Shaped mounds are generally wider than they are long. The slipfaces are on the concave sides of the dunes. These dunes form under winds that blow consistently from one direction, and they also are known as barchans, or transverse dunes.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Shaped mounds are generally wider than they are long. The slipfaces are on the concave sides of the dunes. These dunes form under winds that blow consistently from one direction, and they also are known as barchans, or transverse dunes.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-03-29 10:09:48.0</dcterms:modified>
