New Value=STRATIGRAPHIC SEQUENCE [d845886d-0c44-4505-b5b9-d3fcd819208e,40023] - LAND RECORDS [2bedb6b3-6e92-42e2-b382-60e2a6aab8e9,39979]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from: Press, F. and Siever, R. 1986. Earth. W.H. Freeman and Company.  Fourth Edition. p. 645.  also:  Jackson, J.A., ed. 1997. Glossary of Geology, 4th edition. American Geological  Institute." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of deposited sedimentary beds that reflects the depositional environment of those beds and the geologic history of a region. A stratigraphic sequence is a chronologic succession of sedimentary rocks from older below to younger above without interruption.</skos:definition>
