    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="738185b7-54d6-41a2-b31f-b8a4ee1dabe7"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="89428f01-000f-4d6f-a62b-29dd66b7e8c9"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="efc141a6-7d8e-45d5-b335-2fc122c62d78"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="f5824b8f-c3e7-4e56-96e8-cf4b5adefbf8"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A growing season is the period of the year when crops and other plants grow successfully. The length of the growing season in any given region refers to the number of days when plant growth takes place. The growing season often determines which crops can be grown in an area, as some crops require long growing seasons, while others mature rapidly. Growing season length is limited by many different factors. Depending on the region and the climate, the growing season is influenced by air temperatures, frost days, rainfall, or daylight hours.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-10-08 13:18:07.0</dcterms:modified>
