    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">&apos;Fluvial landforms&apos; are features on the Earth&apos;s surface produced by the action,i.e. erosion and deposition, of a stream or river and include such landforms asbars, levees, braided and meandering channels, and alluvial fans.  &apos;Fluvialprocesses&apos; are those processes included in the action of running water in astream or river</skos:definition>
