New Value=SOIL EROSION [cb21c5cb-cc49-4328-a72d-94ccca1fa888,39859] - LAND SURFACE/AGRICULTURE INDICATORS [112e71ec-c0a1-49a8-82d7-bcb317b45860,39835]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-18 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The wearing away of the land surface by rain or irrigation water, wind, ice, or other natural or anthropogenic agents that abrade, detach and remove geologic parent material or soil from one point on the earth&apos;s surface and deposit it elsewhere, including such processes as gravitational creep and so-called tillage erosion; The detachment and movement of soil or rock by water, wind, ice, or gravity.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="From the Glossary of Soil Terms/Soil Science Society of America (SSSA): http://www.soils.org/sssagloss/" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The wearing away of the land surface by rain or irrigation water, wind, ice, or other natural or anthropogenic agents that abrade, detach and remove geologic parent material or soil from one point on the earth&apos;s surface and deposit it elsewhere, including such processes as gravitational creep and so-called tillage erosion; The detachment and movement of soil or rock by water, wind, ice, or gravity.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-07-18 18:12:54.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
