    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-10-25 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=A set of deposited sedimentary beds that reflects the depositional
environment of those beds and the geologic history of a region. 
A stratigraphic sequence is a chronologic succession of sedimentary rocks from
older below to younger above without interruption.
New Value=A set of deposited sedimentary beds that reflects the depositional
environment of those beds and the geologic history of a region. 
A stratigraphic sequence is a chronologic succession of sedimentary rocks from
older below to younger above without interruption.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-10-25 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Adapted from: Press, F. and Siever, R. 1986. Earth. W.H. Freeman and Company.
Fourth Edition. p. 645. 
also:
Jackson, J.A., ed. 1997. Glossary of Geology, 4th edition. American Geological
Institute.
New Value=Adapted from: Press, F. and Siever, R. 1986. Earth. W.H. Freeman and Company.
Fourth Edition. p. 645. 
also:
Jackson, J.A., ed. 1997. Glossary of Geology, 4th edition. American Geological
Institute.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from: Press, F. and Siever, R. 1986. Earth. W.H. Freeman and Company. Fourth Edition. p. 645.  also: Jackson, J.A., ed. 1997. Glossary of Geology, 4th edition. American Geological Institute." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A set of deposited sedimentary beds that reflects the depositionalenvironment of those beds and the geologic history of a region. A stratigraphic sequence is a chronologic succession of sedimentary rocks fromolder below to younger above without interruption.</skos:definition>
