text: a biome defined by the World Wildlife Fund. The biome includes high altitude grasslands and shrublands around the world. The term &quot;montane&quot; in the name of the biome refers to &quot;high altitude&quot;, rather than the ecological term which denotes the region below treeline.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
