    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="World Wildlife Fund" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">a biome defined by the World Wildlife Fund. The biome includes high altitude grasslands and shrublands around the world. The term &apos;montane&apos; in the name of the biome refers to &apos;high altitude&apos;, rather than the ecological term which denotes the region below treeline.</skos:definition>
