    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">FISH</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
User Note=Definition updated
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Allaby, M. 1998. A Dictionary of Ecology. Oxford University Press.  Oxford, New
York.
New Value=Allaby, M. 1998. A Dictionary of Ecology. Oxford University Press.  Oxford, New York.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
User Note=Definition updated
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Fish are, broadly speaking, any poikilothermic (or organism whose
body temperature varies according to the temperature of its surroundings)
legless, aquatic vertebrate that possesses a series of gills on each side
of the pharynx, a two-chambered heart, no internal nostrils, and at least
a median fin as well as a tail fin.
New Value=Fish are, broadly speaking, any poikilothermic (or organism whose
body temperature varies according to the temperature of its surroundings)
legless, aquatic vertebrate that possesses a series of gills on each side
of the ;pharynx, a two-chambered heart, no internal nostrils, and at least
a median fin as well as a tail fin.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Allaby, M. 1998. A Dictionary of Ecology. Oxford University Press.  Oxford, New York." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="c69cde73-7bd9-489b-a20b-bd23cfb82d92"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="e5404ad9-95bf-4851-9dbb-fecf7dc1e905"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="ed019e00-9b0a-4bdc-89aa-606cc929bd9f"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Fish are, broadly speaking, any poikilothermic (or organism whosebody temperature varies according to the temperature of its surroundings)legless, aquatic vertebrate that possesses a series of gills on each sideof the ;pharynx, a two-chambered heart, no internal nostrils, and at leasta median fin as well as a tail fin.</skos:definition>
