  <skos:Concept rdf:about="f342683b-94ee-4ef6-8915-b18a473fafbd">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="13b8bcd4-7566-49e5-9975-ea15470474ab"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">VOLCANIC ACTIVITY</skos:prefLabel>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Jackson, Julia A. (1997) &lt;i&gt;Glossary of Geology&lt;/i&gt;, 4th Edition.  Alexandria, VA:American Geological Institute, 769 p. &lt;p&gt; For an example, see: &apos;http://www.ssd.noaa.gov/VAAC/washington.html&apos;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Activity pertaining to a vent in the surface of the Earth through which magma
and associated gases and ash erupt.   &lt;br&gt;
A Volcanic Activity Advisory may include reports on erupting volcanoes,
seismic/GPS information that may predict a pending eruption, and volcanic ash.</skos:definition>
