    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from https://www.mikepoweredbydhi.com/products/feflow/groundwater-management" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The management and allocation of groundwater resources foragricultural, industrial, and domestic use. Effective allocation requiresaccurate knowledge about the spatial distribution of existing resourcesand the relevant flow processes. Groundwater management techniquesinclude artificial recharge, aquifer storage and recovery, and watersaving irrigation techniques.</skos:definition>
