    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Coordinate systems enable geographic datasets to use common locations for integration. A coordinate system is a reference system used to represent the locations of geographic features, imagery, and observations, such as Global Positioning System (GPS) locations, within a common geographic framework. A local or regional coordinate system use locally created reference systems to represent the location of geographic features.</skos:definition>
