    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">EARTHQUAKES</skos:prefLabel>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from Jackson, Julia A. (1997) &lt;i&gt;Glossary of Geology, 4th Edition&lt;/i&gt;. Alexandria, VA: American Geological Institute, 769 p. &lt;p&gt; For examples and further explanation:&lt;br&gt; &apos;http://earthquake.usgs.gov/&apos;&lt;br&gt; &apos;http://earthquake.usgs.gov/hazards/probability.html&apos;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A sudden motion or trembling in the Earth caused by the abrupt release of
slowly accumulated strain in the Earth&apos;s lithosphere.&lt;BR&gt; 
An Earthquake Advisory may report on earthquakes occurring in a particular
region and define areas most vulnerable to earthquake damage.</skos:definition>
