    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ISOPRENE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-04-26 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ISOPRENE [9154777e-2e33-49b5-a21e-0a2638c57528,578422] - CARBON AND HYDROCARBON COMPOUNDS [19ab681c-bdd7-4793-bbdb-1ec498575314,575305]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-04-27 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Isoprene is an unsaturated pentahydrocarbon, Isoprene is found in certain plants or obtained by distillation of caoutchouc or gutta-percha. In plants, it is elementary in the formation of isoprenoids, fat-soluble vitamins, carotenoids and related pigments. Isoprenes contribute to flavors and fragrances of essential oils and other plant-derived substances.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/Isoprene" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Isoprene is an unsaturated pentahydrocarbon, Isoprene is found in certain plants or obtained by distillation of caoutchouc or gutta-percha. In plants, it is elementary in the formation of isoprenoids, fat-soluble vitamins, carotenoids and related pigments. Isoprenes contribute to flavors and fragrances of essential oils and other plant-derived substances.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2021-04-27 12:07:20.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="93a95204-8ded-4cde-8937-38e373c41df6">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="19ab681c-bdd7-4793-bbdb-1ec498575314"/>
    <dcterms:created>2022-03-03</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ETHANE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2022-03-03 User Id=sritz Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ETHANE [93a95204-8ded-4cde-8937-38e373c41df6,836064] - CARBON AND HYDROCARBON COMPOUNDS [19ab681c-bdd7-4793-bbdb-1ec498575314,832722]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="National Library of Medicine, https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/ethane" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Ethane appears as a colorless odorless gas. It is easily ignited. The vapors are heavier than air. It can asphyxiate by the displacement of air. Under prolonged exposure to fire or intense heat the containers may rupture violently and rocket. Contact with the liquid may cause frostbite.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="e4781de7-a4a4-4157-a549-4ac238d36512">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="199e3af8-4cf3-48ba-8b28-b9b54756b3db"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SOIL FERTILITY</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-09-30 User Id=tstevens Entity=WeightedRelation Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert WeightedRelation
New Value=id: null
related concept uuid: cdb10789-ef01-46bd-8047-86e550df0df4
relationship type: null
relationship value: null
generated by: null</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="The Nature and Properties of Soils, Prentice Hall, 1996." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The quality of a soil that enables it to provide  essential chemicalelements in quantities and proportions for the growth of specifiedplants.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-09-30 09:36:15.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
    <skos:related rdf:resource="cdb10789-ef01-46bd-8047-86e550df0df4"/>
  </skos:Concept>
