    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Dictionary of Geological Terms, American Geological Institute, 1984." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The reduction in bulk volume or thickness of a soil owing to increasingweight of overlying material that is continually being deposited, or topressures from earth movements, resulting in a decrease of porosity.</skos:definition>
