    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">PRACTICAL SALINITY</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-10-21 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=PRACTICAL SALINITY [9c778b59-6ed9-442e-897e-c48ce5baa3b0,778227] - OCEAN SALINITY [1a4e5774-7d4a-4ce7-9a4c-e2c72c8c377f,778225]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-10-22 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: In the Practical Salinity Scale, practical salinity is defined in terms of the ratio K15 of the electrical conductivity of the seawater sample, at a temperature of 15° C and a pressure of one standard atmosphere, to that of a potassium chloride (KCl) solution, in which the mass fraction of KCl is 32.4356 x 10-3 at the same temperature and pressure.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="http://www.salinityremotesensing.ifremer.fr/sea-surface-salinity/definition-and-units" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">In the Practical Salinity Scale, practical salinity is defined in terms of the ratio K15 of the electrical conductivity of the seawater sample, at a temperature of 15° C and a pressure of one standard atmosphere, to that of a potassium chloride (KCl) solution, in which the mass fraction of KCl is 32.4356 x 10-3 at the same temperature and pressure.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2021-10-22 09:43:04.0</dcterms:modified>
