    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Jackson, J.A., ed. 1997. Glossary of Geology, 4th edition. American Geological Institute." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Radiocarbon refers to radioactive carbon especially carbon-14, but alsocarbon-10 and carbon-12. Carbon-14 is a heavy radioactive isotope of Carbonhaving a mass of 14 and a half-life of 5730 +/-40 years. Carbon-14 is useful indating organic materials during the last 50,000 years.</skos:definition>
