Old Value=Includes Global Change Master Directory detailed variables under the
variable, Vegetation Index: Normalized Difference Vegetation
Index(NDVI).
New Value=An indicator that describes the greenness - the relative density and health of vegetation - for each picture element, or pixel, in a satellite image.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-09-08 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=An indicator that describes the greenness - the relative density and health of vegetation - for each picture element, or pixel, in a satellite image.
New Value=An index that is determined using visible and near-IR channels on AVHRR. Denotes relative chlorophyll content of vegetation during daylight conditions, and is thus used to monitor drought conditions.</skos:changeNote>
