    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="fc77777e-614f-41f1-9b97-d5324fa99105"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An interaction in which a perturbation in one climate quantity causes achange in a second and the change in the second quantity ultimatelyleads to an additional change in the first. A negative feedback is one inwhich the initial perturbation is weakened by the changes it causes; apositive feedback is one in which the initial perturbation is enhanced.The initial perturbation can either be externally forced or arise as part ofinternal variability.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2019-05-30 08:26:56.0</dcterms:modified>
