    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">RADIOCARBON</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=gee-cee Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=RADIOCARBON [8f4e90e0-aea0-40cd-b781-a6a69a6e6cb3,40013] - LAND RECORDS [2bedb6b3-6e92-42e2-b382-60e2a6aab8e9,39979]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-23 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Radiocarbon refers to radioactive carbon especially carbon-14, but also carbon-10 and carbon-12. Carbon-14 is a heavy radioactive isotope of Carbon having a mass of 14 and a half-life of 5730 +/-40 years. Carbon-14 is useful in dating organic materials during the last 50,000 years.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Jackson, J.A., ed. 1997. Glossary of Geology, 4th edition. American Geological Institute." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Radiocarbon refers to radioactive carbon especially carbon-14, but also carbon-10 and carbon-12. Carbon-14 is a heavy radioactive isotope of Carbon having a mass of 14 and a half-life of 5730 +/-40 years. Carbon-14 is useful in dating organic materials during the last 50,000 years.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-07-23 17:26:53.0</dcterms:modified>
