System Note=update Definition
Old Value=A plant nutrient usually found in relatively small amounts(&lt;100 mg
kg-1) in plants.  These are usually B, Cl, Cu, Fe, Mn, Mo, Ni, Co, and
Zn.  In environmental applications it is those elements exclusive of the eight
abundant rock-forming elements: oxygen, aluminum, silicon, iron, calcium,
sodium, potassium, and magnesium.
New Value=A plant nutrient usually found in relatively small amounts(&lt;100 mg
kg-1) in plants.  These are usually B, Cl, Cu, Fe, Mn, Mo, Ni, Co, and
Zn.  In environmental applications it is those elements exclusive of the eight
abundant rock-forming elements: oxygen, aluminum, silicon, iron, calcium,
sodium, potassium, and magnesium.</skos:changeNote>
