    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of soil Sciece Terms, 1996.  Soil Science Society of America, Madison, WI. &apos;http://www.soils.org/sssagloss/&apos;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A plant nutrient usually found in relatively small amounts(&lt;100 mgkg-1) in plants.  These are usually B, Cl, Cu, Fe, Mn, Mo, Ni, Co, andZn.  In environmental applications it is those elements exclusive of the eightabundant rock-forming elements: oxygen, aluminum, silicon, iron, calcium,sodium, potassium, and magnesium.</skos:definition>
