    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-08-20 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A form of erosion caused by the force of moving water currents rushing into a crack in the rockface. It is strong enough to loosen sediment along the river bed and banks. The water compresses the air in the crack, pushing it right to the back.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A form of erosion caused by the force of moving water currents rushing into a crack in the rockface. It is strong enough to loosen sediment along the river bed and banks. The water compresses the air in the crack, pushing it right to the back.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-10-11 14:18:03.0</dcterms:modified>
