    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">WIND CHILL INDEX</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-09-04 User Id=epneff Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=WIND CHILL INDEX [d50d0685-f42f-4693-9458-eddb9ccf5704,105833] - ATMOSPHERIC TEMPERATURE INDICES [25d73bcf-c8d4-4c0e-ac98-8f3e98677e73,105815]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2014-04-14 User Id=128.183.164.42 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Added definition
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A means of quantifying the threat of rapid cooling during breezy or windy conditions that may result in hypothermia in cold conditions.

The index is used to remind the public to minimize exposure when outdoors and to take precautionary actions.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 2012,  http://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/Wind-chill_index" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A means of quantifying the threat of rapid cooling during breezy or windy conditions that may result in hypothermia in cold conditions.The index is used to remind the public to minimize exposure when outdoors and to take precautionary actions.</skos:definition>
