System Note=add broader relation
New Value=BOREHOLES [f1f84fc8-d242-4f97-bb7d-77b68631273e,39981] - LAND RECORDS [2bedb6b3-6e92-42e2-b382-60e2a6aab8e9,39979]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-23 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Boreholes are holes drilled deep into the ground (or ocean crust). Profiles of rock temperatures with depth can be related to the history of temperature changes at the surface, which can be converted to estimates of air temperature. Borehole temperature measurements can provide estimates of local temperature variations over time intervals of a few hundred to over a thousand years.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Burroughs, William J. 2001. Climate Change: A Multidisciplinary Approach. Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, UK." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Boreholes are holes drilled deep into the ground (or ocean crust). Profiles of rock temperatures with depth can be related to the history of temperature changes at the surface, which can be converted to estimates of air temperature. Borehole temperature measurements can provide estimates of local temperature variations over time intervals of a few hundred to over a thousand years.</skos:definition>
