    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">TROPOSPHERIC TEMPERATURE ANOMALIES</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-25 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=TROPOSPHERIC TEMPERATURE ANOMALIES [f0e47cca-fa6e-44d0-b900-43920a3d0b91,39787] - TEMPERATURE INDICATORS [2dcffd8f-2b01-4c68-a4f2-c4940d2709a3,39777]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-09-23 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Refers to temperature anomalies in the troposphere. A temperature anomaly means a departure from a reference value or long-term average. A positive anomaly indicates that the observed temperature was warmer than the reference value, while a negative anomaly indicates that the observed temperature was cooler than the reference value.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://www.ncei.noaa.gov/access/monitoring/global-temperature-anomalies" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Refers to temperature anomalies in the troposphere. A temperature anomaly means a departure from a reference value or long-term average. A positive anomaly indicates that the observed temperature was warmer than the reference value, while a negative anomaly indicates that the observed temperature was cooler than the reference value.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-09-23 11:09:29.0</dcterms:modified>
