  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="9bad3c7b-daf6-428a-89bd-ce62b074dfcf">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="3526afb8-0dc9-43c7-8ad4-f34f250a1e91"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">CATION EXCHANGE CAPACITY</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-10 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=The sum of exchangeable bases plus total soil acidity at a specific pH value
usually 7.0 or 8.0. When acidity is expressed as salt extractable acidity, the
cation exchange capacity (CEC) is called the effective cation exchange
capacity(ECEC) because this is considered to be the CEC of the exchanger at the
native pH value. It is usually expressed in centimoles of charge per kilogram
of exchanger.
New Value=The sum of exchangeable bases plus total soil acidity at a specific pH value usually 7.0 or 8.0. When acidity is expressed as salt extractable acidity, the cation exchange capacity (CEC) is called the effective cation exchange capacity(ECEC) because this is considered to be the CEC of the exchanger at the native pH value. It is usually expressed in centimoles of charge per kilogram of exchanger.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-10 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Jackson, J.A. (1997) &lt;i&gt;Glossary of Geology.&lt;/i&gt; 4th ed. Alexandria,
VA:American Geological Institute. 769 p.
New Value=Jackson, J.A. (1997) Glossary of Geology. 4th ed. Alexandria, VA:American Geological Institute. 769 p.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-09-26 User Id=tstevens Entity=WeightedRelation Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert WeightedRelation
New Value=id: null
related concept uuid: 5c05e69f-f6db-4296-abd3-3b07e6093579
relationship type: null
relationship value: null
generated by: null</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Jackson, J.A. (1997) Glossary of Geology. 4th ed. Alexandria, VA:American Geological Institute. 769 p." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The sum of exchangeable bases plus total soil acidity at a specific pH value usually 7.0 or 8.0. When acidity is expressed as salt extractable acidity, the cation exchange capacity (CEC) is called the effective cation exchange capacity(ECEC) because this is considered to be the CEC of the exchanger at the native pH value. It is usually expressed in centimoles of charge per kilogram of exchanger.</skos:definition>
