  <skos:Concept rdf:about="d2e93932-0231-4b23-af2f-217c6315a95e">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="3487d350-a5a5-43d9-a60d-c1407dd2f0ce"/>
    <dcterms:created>2013-02-14</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ABSORPTION</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-21 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The process in which incident radiant energy is retained by a substance.

A further process always results from absorption, that is, the irreversible conversion of the absorbed radiation into some other form of energy within and according to the nature of the absorbing medium. The absorbing medium itself may emit radiation, but only after an energy conversion has occurred.
See attenuation.

The taking up or assimilation of one substance by another.

The substances may combine chemically, or the absorption may just correspond to a physical solubility.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-02-14 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ABSORPTION [d2e93932-0231-4b23-af2f-217c6315a95e,82301] - CLOUD RADIATIVE TRANSFER [3487d350-a5a5-43d9-a60d-c1407dd2f0ce,82135]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="American Meteorological Society (http://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/Main_Page)" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The process in which incident radiant energy is retained by a substance.A further process always results from absorption, that is, the irreversible conversion of the absorbed radiation into some other form of energy within and according to the nature of the absorbing medium. The absorbing medium itself may emit radiation, but only after an energy conversion has occurred.See attenuation.The taking up or assimilation of one substance by another.The substances may combine chemically, or the absorption may just correspond to a physical solubility.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-03-21 14:46:27.0</dcterms:modified>
