    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-04-21 User Id=sritz Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Huschke, R.E. 1959. Glossary of Meteorology. American Meteorological
Association, Boston, MA. See also: Pickard, G.L. and W.J. Emery. 1990.
Descriptive Physical Oceanography: An Introduction. Pergamon Press, NY
New Value=Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The physical process by which a liquid or solid is transformed to the gaseous state; the opposite of condensation.</skos:definition>
