    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ARETES</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-04-01 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: An arete is a thin, almost knife-like, ridge of rock which is typically formed when two glaciers erode parallel U-shaped valleys. The arête is a thin ridge of rock that is left separating the two valleys.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-05 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ARETES [8e73bff6-c2f9-46a6-963b-8ef09dd7f5f3,82725] - GLACIAL LANDFORMS [3c78951a-0293-4fb0-baff-ec7372fe784d,64133]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An arete is a thin, almost knife-like, ridge of rock which is typically formed when two glaciers erode parallel U-shaped valleys. The arête is a thin ridge of rock that is left separating the two valleys.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-04-01 09:46:56.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="d8aee072-097c-496f-8fe7-b65605fc1103">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="39f5a91f-c5b6-4aa9-a0c6-05530306f17b"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">TIDES</skos:prefLabel>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from: &apos;http://gcmd.nasa.gov/md/Def_DB/OCEANS_TIDES.html&apos;  &apos;http://www.env.gov.sg/info/press/pr2001/rel-23-2001.html&apos;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Reports providing information pertaining to the study of the periodic rise andfall of the sea surface, generated by long-wavelength waves that are caused bythe interaction of gravitational force and inertia. Variables includecharacteristics of tides and other aspects important to their study.</skos:definition>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="cfaf76ef-89e2-4dc8-a4eb-b3308ef8c52c">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="3ab3aa92-9cca-4660-a0ed-281fff07eede"/>
    <dcterms:created>2013-08-05</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SALTATION</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-08-20 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A specific type of particle transport by fluids such as wind, or the denser fluid water. It occurs when loose material is removed from a bed and carried by the fluid, before being transported back to the surface.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-08-05 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=SALTATION [cfaf76ef-89e2-4dc8-a4eb-b3308ef8c52c,105443] - AEOLIAN PROCESSES [3ab3aa92-9cca-4660-a0ed-281fff07eede,84207]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A specific type of particle transport by fluids such as wind, or the denser fluid water. It occurs when loose material is removed from a bed and carried by the fluid, before being transported back to the surface.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-08-20 10:13:48.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="edfbff1e-b24b-40b9-be54-e1823b4d7f49">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="3f4cfc81-7745-43d9-b313-f68cdf72359b"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">FOSSIL FUEL BURNING</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Chiras, Daniel D. 1998. Environmental Science.	A Systems Approach to
Sustainable Development. Wadsworth Publishing Company. Belmont, California.
New Value=Chiras, Daniel D. 1998. Environmental Science. A Systems Approach to Sustainable Development. Wadsworth Publishing Company. Belmont, California.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Fossil fuel burning refers to the burning of any one of the organic
fuels (coal, natural gas, oil, tar sands, and oil shale) derived from once
living plants or animals.
New Value=Fossil fuel burning refers to the burning of any one of the organic fuels (coal, natural gas, oil, tar sands, and oil shale) derived from once living plants or animals.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Chiras, Daniel D. 1998. Environmental Science. A Systems Approach to Sustainable Development. Wadsworth Publishing Company. Belmont, California." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Fossil fuel burning refers to the burning of any one of the organic fuels (coal, natural gas, oil, tar sands, and oil shale) derived from once living plants or animals.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-07-11 10:00:12.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="a8bfc8ad-42f2-43cc-b161-20058037bb95">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="3c78951a-0293-4fb0-baff-ec7372fe784d"/>
    <dcterms:created>2013-03-05</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">OUTWASH FANS/PLAINS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-04-01 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: An outwash fan is a fan-shaped body of sediments deposited by braided streams from a melting glacier. Sediment locked within the ice of the glacier, gets transported by the streams of meltwater, and deposits on the outwash plain, at the terminus of the glacier.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-05 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=OUTWASH FANS/PLAINS [a8bfc8ad-42f2-43cc-b161-20058037bb95,82773] - GLACIAL LANDFORMS [3c78951a-0293-4fb0-baff-ec7372fe784d,64133]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An outwash fan is a fan-shaped body of sediments deposited by braided streams from a melting glacier. Sediment locked within the ice of the glacier, gets transported by the streams of meltwater, and deposits on the outwash plain, at the terminus of the glacier.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-04-01 10:35:16.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
