    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">CALCIUM</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2018-03-07 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: An alkaline earth metal, calcium is a reactive pale yellow metal that forms a dark oxide-nitride layer when exposed to air. Its physical and chemical properties are most similar to its heavier homologues strontium and barium. It is the fifth most abundant element in Earth&apos;s crust and the third most abundant metal, after iron and aluminum.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2018-03-07 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=CALCIUM [e5a658d5-74db-4022-894f-edc8d297767a,310653] - CONTAMINANTS [42c6d91b-afef-4638-95c5-0d130828b2e7,84623]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="World Health Organization" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An alkaline earth metal, calcium is a reactive pale yellow metal that forms a dark oxide-nitride layer when exposed to air. Its physical and chemical properties are most similar to its heavier homologues strontium and barium. It is the fifth most abundant element in Earth&apos;s crust and the third most abundant metal, after iron and aluminum.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2018-03-07 09:18:36.0</dcterms:modified>
