    <skos:changeNote>Date=2018-03-07 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Minerals are solid, naturally occurring inorganic substances that can be found in the earth’s crust. They are formed without the intervention of humans and have a definite chemical composition and crystal structure.

Metals are elementary substances, such as gold, silver and copper that are crystalline when solid and naturally occurring in minerals. They often have the characteristics of being good conductors of electricity and heat, of being shiny in appearance and of being malleable
New Value=Minerals are solid, naturally occurring inorganic substances that can be found in the earth’s crust. They are formed without the intervention of humans and have a definite chemical composition and crystal structure.

Metals are elementary substances, such as gold, silver and copper that are crystalline when solid and naturally occurring in minerals. They often have the characteristics of being good conductors of electricity and heat, of being shiny in appearance and of being malleable.</skos:changeNote>
