    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-24 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Pertaining to the measurement of isotopic (excluding oxygen) signatures in ocean/lake sediments to determine past climatic conditions, and apply those findings to the Earth&apos;s climate at the time period in question. Carbon isotope analysis is very important in extracting paleoclimatic signatures from corals and from benthic forams.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Bradley, R.S. 1999. Paleoclimatology: Reconstructing Climates of the Quaternary, 2nd edition. Harcourt Academic Press." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Pertaining to the measurement of isotopic (excluding oxygen) signatures in ocean/lake sediments to determine past climatic conditions, and apply those findings to the Earth&apos;s climate at the time period in question. Carbon isotope analysis is very important in extracting paleoclimatic signatures from corals and from benthic forams.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-10-23 15:26:04.0</dcterms:modified>
