    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ISOTOPIC ANALYSIS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=gee-cee Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add narrower relation
New Value=ISOTOPIC ANALYSIS [bd1834b0-4f8f-4616-b330-6205bff567c2,39971] - CARBON ISOTOPE [437f13e8-0b8a-44a2-a7fd-5b41a00299db,39973]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=gee-cee Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add narrower relation
New Value=ISOTOPIC ANALYSIS [bd1834b0-4f8f-4616-b330-6205bff567c2,39971] - OXYGEN ISOTOPE [e91ff41a-5cf5-460b-b765-c553ca2a4ae2,39975]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-19 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The isotopic record found in various non-marine records reveal direct
information about the past climate. d18O (delta oxygen-18), 16O and 18O are isotopes of oxygen with slight differences in atomic weight. Studies using other isotopes such as Carbon-13, Carbon-14 and Hydrogen are widely used. Isoptopic analysis is especially important in dendroclimatologic and speleothem analyses.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=gee-cee Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ISOTOPIC ANALYSIS [bd1834b0-4f8f-4616-b330-6205bff567c2,39971] - TREE RINGS [6444fc67-8cad-41c0-9ded-e93f604ba8b0,39969]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=gee-cee Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add narrower relation
New Value=ISOTOPIC ANALYSIS [bd1834b0-4f8f-4616-b330-6205bff567c2,39971] - HYDROGEN ISOTOPE [89387757-3548-4fe0-a383-d8f935f07c71,39977]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Eddy, J.A. and H. Oeschger, eds. 1993. Global Changes in the Perspective of the Past. Dahlem Workshop Reports, Environmental Sciences Research Report 12, J. Wiley." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="437f13e8-0b8a-44a2-a7fd-5b41a00299db"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="89387757-3548-4fe0-a383-d8f935f07c71"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="e91ff41a-5cf5-460b-b765-c553ca2a4ae2"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The isotopic record found in various non-marine records reveal directinformation about the past climate. d18O (delta oxygen-18), 16O and 18O are isotopes of oxygen with slight differences in atomic weight. Studies using other isotopes such as Carbon-13, Carbon-14 and Hydrogen are widely used. Isoptopic analysis is especially important in dendroclimatologic and speleothem analyses.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-07-19 16:39:37.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
