    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">REFLECTION</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-10 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A method of exploration geophysics that uses the principles of seismology to estimate of the properties of the Earth&apos;s subsurface from reflected seismic waves. This measurement is also known as seismic reflection.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-05 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=REFLECTION [9911bf57-9d52-4fb3-a915-9e522e9845d5,83085] - NON-METALLIC MINERAL PHYSICAL/OPTICAL PROPERTIES [42424cb5-aa02-4e7e-b164-b2a3324285c6,83059]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Sheriff, R. E., Geldart, L. P., (1995), 2nd Edition. Exploration Seismology. Cambridge University Press" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A method of exploration geophysics that uses the principles of seismology to estimate of the properties of the Earth&apos;s subsurface from reflected seismic waves. This measurement is also known as seismic reflection.</skos:definition>
