System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A lustrous, brittle, hard metal. Its color is silver-gray and it can be highly polished. It does not tarnish in air. When heated it borns and forms the green chromic oxide. Chromium is unstable in oxygen. It immediately produces a thin oxide layer that is impermeable to oxygen and protects the metal below.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Reviews of Modern Physics" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A lustrous, brittle, hard metal. Its color is silver-gray and it can be highly polished. It does not tarnish in air. When heated it borns and forms the green chromic oxide. Chromium is unstable in oxygen. It immediately produces a thin oxide layer that is impermeable to oxygen and protects the metal below.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2018-03-07 09:20:41.0</dcterms:modified>
