    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Burroughs, William J. 2001. Climate Change: A Multidisciplinary Approach. Cambridge University Press, Cambridge, UK." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Boreholes are holes drilled deep into the ground (or ocean crust). Profiles ofrock temperatures with depth can be related to the history of temperaturechanges at the surface, which can be converted to estimates of air temperature.Borehhole temperature measurements can provide estimates of local temperaturevariations over time intervals of a few hundred to over a thousand years.</skos:definition>
