    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SEDIMENT CORE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2020-05-18 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=SEDIMENT CORE [a088eccf-1160-4f01-ab71-53e720264ecd,560149] - OCEAN/LAKE RECORDS [45325a01-2522-48d3-bffa-0edf1a934d48,84397]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="ROTH&apos;WELL, R.G. 2006. New Techniques in Sediment Core Analysis. Geological Society, London, Special Publications, 267, 1-29. 0305-8719/06/$15.00 9 The Geological Society of London 2006." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">tube of sediment collected from the bed of a water body, allowing the analysis of layers of which it is made up, leading to information on seabed / lakebed character, depositional history and environmental change.</skos:definition>
