User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ALTOSTRATUS [f58d0203-0070-422c-ab52-6ca8ffbb6362,82187] - TROPOSPHERIC/MID-LEVEL CLOUDS (OBSERVED/ANALYZED) [a413f88b-859c-4035-a45b-2faa9934156b,82125]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-20 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A principal cloud type, forming in the middle levels of the troposphere, and appearing as a grey or bluish sheet. In aviation forecasts and reports it is coded as AS.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-02-14 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add narrower relation
New Value=ALTOSTRATUS [f58d0203-0070-422c-ab52-6ca8ffbb6362,82187] - ALTOSTRATUS UNDULATUS [4da38a31-aac6-4080-96b0-c8ee2cb33158,82189]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Bureau of Meteorology: REFERENCE MATERIAL: Glossary of Weather Terms" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="4da38a31-aac6-4080-96b0-c8ee2cb33158"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A principal cloud type, forming in the middle levels of the troposphere, and appearing as a grey or bluish sheet. In aviation forecasts and reports it is coded as AS.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-03-20 17:02:02.0</dcterms:modified>
