    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-05 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=LATERAL MORAINE [a4f0e7c2-711e-4675-b7c8-f5430905aa89,82763] - MORAINES [4f590d94-110c-4762-9171-aba6d24af6a0,82759]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-04-01 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Parallel ridges of debris deposited along the sides of a glacier. The unconsolidated debris can be deposited on top of the glacier by frost shattering of the valley walls and from tributary streams flowing into the valley.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Parallel ridges of debris deposited along the sides of a glacier. The unconsolidated debris can be deposited on top of the glacier by frost shattering of the valley walls and from tributary streams flowing into the valley.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-04-01 10:30:43.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="ca464924-4299-46ea-8cae-fd9bad49c1b1">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="f0bd7eeb-9004-4e40-a649-f6010d8a4303"/>
    <dcterms:created>2013-02-18</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ISOSTATIC UPLIFT</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-04-02 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Refers to the the gradual uplift following rapid erosional removal of material from a mountain range. The land rises as a result of the removal of the weight. Another example of isostatic uplift is post-glacial rebound following the melting of continental glaciers and ice sheets.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-02-18 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ISOSTATIC UPLIFT [ca464924-4299-46ea-8cae-fd9bad49c1b1,82545] - TECTONIC PROCESSES [f0bd7eeb-9004-4e40-a649-f6010d8a4303,82507]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-10-31 User Id=tstevens Entity=WeightedRelation Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert WeightedRelation
New Value=id: null
related concept uuid: 4f0f52fb-b272-49c6-9425-690d9285c380
relationship type: null
relationship value: null
generated by: null</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="tectonic-forces.org" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Refers to the the gradual uplift following rapid erosional removal of material from a mountain range. The land rises as a result of the removal of the weight. Another example of isostatic uplift is post-glacial rebound following the melting of continental glaciers and ice sheets.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-10-31 08:05:00.0</dcterms:modified>
