New Value=id: null
text: Division Pteridophyta. Class Lycopodiopsida. Order Lycopodiales. Lycopodium, commonly called club mosses, are asexual, flowerless, vascular plants with widely branched stems and needle-like leaves.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://www2.mcdaniel.edu/Biology/botf99/earlyplants/page4aly.html" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Division Pteridophyta. Class Lycopodiopsida. Order Lycopodiales. Lycopodium, commonly called club mosses, are asexual, flowerless, vascular plants with widely branched stems and needle-like leaves.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2017-03-15 11:06:40.0</dcterms:modified>
