    <skos:broader rdf:resource="5a7bb095-4d12-4232-bc75-b8e82197cb92"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">VIRTUAL TEMPERATURE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-10-16 User Id=saritz Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
User Note=updated definition
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Glossary of Weather and Climate, American Meteorological Society, 1996.
New Value=Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 2013, http://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/Virtual_temperature</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-09-04 User Id=epneff Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Move Concepts
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=VIRTUAL TEMPERATURE [fd19a3f1-8eeb-49ab-bcaf-e7b4b267d415,85675] - SURFACE TEMPERATURE [5a7bb095-4d12-4232-bc75-b8e82197cb92,86389]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-10-16 User Id=saritz Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
User Note=updated definition
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=In a system of humid air, the temperature of dry air having the same
density and pressure as the humid air.
New Value=(Also called density temperature.) The virtual temperature Tv = T(1 + rv/ ε)/(1 + rv), where rv is the mixing ratio and ε is the ratio of the gas constants of air and water vapor, ≈ 0.622.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-09-04 User Id=epneff Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=DELETE 
User Note=Move Concepts
System Note=delete broader relation
Old Value=VIRTUAL TEMPERATURE [fd19a3f1-8eeb-49ab-bcaf-e7b4b267d415,85675] - ATMOSPHERIC TEMPERATURE [35e1f93b-99b3-4430-b477-0ecafa80d67a,83865]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 2013, http://glossary.ametsoc.org/wiki/Virtual_temperature" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">(Also called density temperature.) The virtual temperature Tv = T(1 + rv/ ε)/(1 + rv), where rv is the mixing ratio and ε is the ratio of the gas constants of air and water vapor, ≈ 0.622.</skos:definition>
