    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">CONDENSATION</skos:prefLabel>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Huschke, R.E. 1959. Glossary of Meteorology. American Meteorological Association, Boston, MA. See also: Pickard, G.L. and W.J. Emery. 1990. Descriptive Physical Oceanography: An Introduction. Pergamon Press, NY" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The physical process by which a vapor becomes a liquid or solid. In theheat budget of the ocean, the rate of heat gain can be affected by thecondensation.</skos:definition>
