    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
User Note=Definition updated
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Diatoms are algae of the Phylum Ochrista that lack flagella.  They have
a jewel-like appearance.	They play an extremely important role in
aquatic food webs in that they are the second most abundant component of
marine plankton (after blue-green algae).
New Value=Diatoms are algae of the Phylum Ochrista that lack flagella.  They have
a jewel-like appearance.	They play an extremely important role in
aquatic food webs in that they are the second most abundant component of
marine plankton (after blue-green algae).</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Gould, J. and W.Keaton. 1996. Biological Science. W.W. Norton and Company. New York, New York." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Diatoms are algae of the Phylum Ochrista that lack flagella.  They havea jewel-like appearance.	They play an extremely important role inaquatic food webs in that they are the second most abundant component ofmarine plankton (after blue-green algae).</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2017-03-15 11:12:10.0</dcterms:modified>
