    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A crack in an ice sheet or glacier (compare to crevice, which is in rock). Crevasses often have vertical or near-vertical walls, which can then melt and create seracs, arches, etc.; these walls sometimes expose layers that represent the glacier&apos;s stratigraphy.</skos:definition>
