    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from the USGCRP Glossary (https://www.globalchange.gov/climate-change/glossary) and the European Environment Agency Phenology of plant and animal species (https://www.eea.europa.eu/data-and-maps/indicators/plant-phenology-2) indicator" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="c6f81edb-b683-4356-93e6-5852766a5ee8"/>
    <skos:narrower rdf:resource="f73cf4ee-2ae0-47b0-a294-5f8a8f694215"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Changes in the temporal pattern of seasonal life cycle events in plantsand animals, such as timing of blooming, hibernation, and migration.Some phenological responses are triggered by mean temperature,while others are more responsive to day length or weather. Changes inphenology affect the growing season and, thus, ecosystem functioningand productivity.</skos:definition>
