    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
User Note=Definition updated
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Peatlands are areas formed by a brown mass of organic matter in which
twigs, roots, and other plant parts can still be recognized.  These areas
formed due to lack of enough oxygen to decay vegetation completely on
land. Peatlands form in fresh-water swamps, indicated by the plant
fossils.
New Value=Peatlands are areas formed by a brown mass of organic matter in which twigs, roots, and other plant parts can still be recognized.  These areas formed due to lack of enough oxygen to decay vegetation completely on land. Peatlands form in fresh-water swamps, indicated by the plant fossils.</skos:changeNote>
