    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Phylum Mollusca. Class Bivalvia.  Sedentary bivalve characterized by two-part shell of calcium carbonate secreted by the mantle and joined by a ligamentous hinge held shut by adductor muscles distinguished by slipper dark colored shells and attached to strata by byssus.</skos:definition>
