    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">EPIDEMIOLOGY</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-29 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The study of factors affecting the health and illness of populations, and serves as the foundation and logic of interventions made in the interest of public health and preventative medicine. In the study of communicable and non-communicable diseases, the work of epidemiologists ranges from outbreak investigation to study design, data collection and analysis including the development of statistical models to test hypotheses. Epidemiologists also study the interaction of diseases in a population, a condition known as a syndemic.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add narrower relation
