    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Definition added
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Changes in crystal-orientation fabric, changes in conductivity or changes in the amount of bubbles (respectively density) are considered to cause internal reflections in glaciers and ice sheets
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Eisen, O., et al. 2003. Geophysical Research Letters. &apos;Revealing the nature of radar reflections in ice: DEP-based FDTD forward modeling&apos; Vol 30, No 5, 1218, doi:10.1029/2002GL016403" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Changes in crystal-orientation fabric, changes in conductivity or changes in the amount of bubbles (respectively density) are considered to cause internal reflections in glaciers and ice sheets</skos:definition>
