    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">LARVACEANS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-13 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Definition added
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Class Appendicularia, Phylum Chordata, commonly called larvaceans are solitary, free-swimming tunicates characterized by a transparent body of a trunk housing internal organs and a tail with a notochord. The trunk secretes a mucous house that encloses the animal therefore making it a gelatinous zooplankton
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="speciesidentification.org" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Class Appendicularia, Phylum Chordata, commonly called larvaceans are solitary, free-swimming tunicates characterized by a transparent body of a trunk housing internal organs and a tail with a notochord. The trunk secretes a mucous house that encloses the animal therefore making it a gelatinous zooplankton</skos:definition>
