text: The monomers of organic compounds join together by a chemical reaction know as dehydration synthesis to make polymers. The reverse reaction of breaking up polymers is accomplished by another chemical reaction known as hyrdolysis.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Biology Department, Lone Star College—North Harris Campus" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The monomers of organic compounds join together by a chemical reaction know as dehydration synthesis to make polymers. The reverse reaction of breaking up polymers is accomplished by another chemical reaction known as hyrdolysis.</skos:definition>
