    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Food and Agriculture Organization (FAO) Fisheries Glossary, http://www.fao.org/fi/glossary/" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The farming of aquatic organisms including fish, molluscs, crustaceans andaquatic plants with some sort of intervention in the rearing process to enhanceproduction, such as regular stocking, feeding, protection from predators, etc. Also referred to as Mariculture - Marine fish farming (aquaculture). Raising ofmarine animals and plants in the controlled or selected aquatic environmentsfor any commercial, recreational, or public purpose.</skos:definition>
