    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A steep conical hill composed of glaciofluvial sediments. This feature develops when glacial crevasses and depressions in stagnant glacial ice are filled with sand and gravel deposits from sediment loaded meltwater.</skos:definition>
