    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-25 User Id=mpmorahan Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add narrower relation
New Value=ARCTIC OSCILLATION [98e5a7e4-b946-474a-8214-c1b7b3e5f976,22325] - AO [a135fceb-cf13-4186-9ad3-8d5db82312c9,39703]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Joint Institute for the Study of the Atmosphere and Ocean, U. Washington http://jisao.washington.edu/ao/" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Arctic Oscillation (AO) is the dominant pattern of non-seasonal
sea-level pressure (SLP) variations north of 20N, and it is
characterized by SLP anomalies of one sign in the Arctic and anomalies
of opposite sign centered about 37-45N. Additional information is
available for the Arctic Oscillation (AO) and for the North Atlantic
Oscillation (NAO), a close relative of the AO 
(http://jisao.washington.edu/ao/)</skos:definition>
