    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">NATIONAL SANITATION FOUNDATION WATER QUALITY INDEX</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2018-03-07 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A water quality index developed by the National Sanitation Foundation (NSF) in 1970 which provides a standardized method for comparing the water quality of various bodies of water. There are nine water quality parameters included in the index: dissolved oxygen (DO), fecal coliform, pH, biochemical oxygen demand (BOD) (5-day), temperature change (from 1 mile upstream), total phosphate, nitrate, turbidity, total solids.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2018-03-07 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=NATIONAL SANITATION FOUNDATION WATER QUALITY INDEX [989e0558-a5fb-4758-bb82-c7d0a6a9f319,310707] - WATER QUALITY INDEXES [f2130ca3-3587-4312-b6d4-138456b5ea78,310635]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="http://bcn.boulder.co.us/basin/watershed/wqi_nsf.html" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A water quality index developed by the National Sanitation Foundation (NSF) in 1970 which provides a standardized method for comparing the water quality of various bodies of water. There are nine water quality parameters included in the index: dissolved oxygen (DO), fecal coliform, pH, biochemical oxygen demand (BOD) (5-day), temperature change (from 1 mile upstream), total phosphate, nitrate, turbidity, total solids.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2018-03-07 12:58:49.0</dcterms:modified>
