    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://agupubs.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1002/2015JC011145" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The mean dynamic topography (MDT) is the height of the time-mean sea surface above the geoid. Its slope reveals the magnitude and direction of ocean surface geostrophic currents; hence, it is a surface representation of the ocean&apos;s mean circulation.</skos:definition>
