    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SULFUR HEXAFLUORIDE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-02-26 User Id=tstevens Entity=NarrowerRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add narrower relation
New Value=SULFUR HEXAFLUORIDE [b4c7dec8-6a9a-4424-8f80-4ad1ed0bc5ec,560883] - SULFUR HEXAFLUORIDE SURFACE [fceaf7e0-c22b-40a1-ba1d-37616031dba6,560885]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-03-03 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Sulfur hexafluoride is an extremely potent and persistent greenhouse gas that is primarily utilized as an electrical insulator and arc suppressant. It is inorganic, colorless, odorless, non-flammable, and non-toxic. SF6 has an octahedral geometry, consisting of six fluorine atoms attached to a central sulfur atom. It is a hypervalent molecule.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
