    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The formation of mountain ranges by intense upward displacement of the earth&apos;s crust, usually associated with folding, thrust faulting, and other compressional processes.</skos:definition>
