    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Pertaining to chemical process by which electrons are added or removed from an
atom.
New Value=Describes all chemical reactions in which atoms have their oxidation number (oxidation state) changed. This can be either a simple redox process, such as the oxidation of carbon to yield carbon dioxide (CO2) or the reduction of carbon by hydrogen to yield methane (CH4), or a complex process such as the oxidation of sugar (C6H12O6) in the human body through a series of complex electron transfer processes.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="American Chemical Society" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Describes all chemical reactions in which atoms have their oxidation number (oxidation state) changed. This can be either a simple redox process, such as the oxidation of carbon to yield carbon dioxide (CO2) or the reduction of carbon by hydrogen to yield methane (CH4), or a complex process such as the oxidation of sugar (C6H12O6) in the human body through a series of complex electron transfer processes.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-03-11 13:25:40.0</dcterms:modified>
