    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SEA ANEMONES</skos:prefLabel>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Gould, J. and W.Keaton. 1996. Biological Science. W.W. Norton and Company. New York, New York." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Anemones, or Sea Anemones, belong to the class Anthozoa, which are
sedentary polypoid forms including sea fans, and hard and soft corals.
Anthozoans are the most advanced members of the Phylum Cnidaria.</skos:definition>
