    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Definition added
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Phylum Chordata. Class Mammalia. Order Chiroptera. Bats forelimbs form wedded wings with long spread-out digits covered by a thin membrane flapped in flying making them the only mammals capable of sustained flight. Bats have a highly adapted lung system, use echolocation as they have poorly developed eyes and most are nocturnal
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Bat Conservation International" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Phylum Chordata. Class Mammalia. Order Chiroptera. Bats forelimbs form wedded wings with long spread-out digits covered by a thin membrane flapped in flying making them the only mammals capable of sustained flight. Bats have a highly adapted lung system, use echolocation as they have poorly developed eyes and most are nocturnal</skos:definition>
