    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">SUBDUCTION</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-10-21 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A geological process in which the oceanic lithosphere is recycled into the Earth&apos;s mantle at convergent boundaries. Where the oceanic lithosphere of a tectonic plate converges with the less dense lithosphere of a second plate, the heavier plate dives beneath the second plate and sinks into the mantle.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2021-10-20 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=SUBDUCTION [c6f748f7-3a2a-4c76-90bd-8e8d7a691b21,778211] - OCEAN CIRCULATION [a031952d-9f00-4ba5-9966-5f87ab9dfdd4,775052]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Stern, Robert J. (2002), &apos;Subduction zones&apos;, Reviews of Geophysics, 40 (4): 1012, Bibcode:2002RvGeo..40.1012S, doi:10.1029/2001RG000108" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A geological process in which the oceanic lithosphere is recycled into the Earth&apos;s mantle at convergent boundaries. Where the oceanic lithosphere of a tectonic plate converges with the less dense lithosphere of a second plate, the heavier plate dives beneath the second plate and sinks into the mantle.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2021-10-21 15:41:14.0</dcterms:modified>
