    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="National Snow and Ice Data Center CIRES/University of Colorado" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Natural nitrogen (N) consists of two stable isotopes, nitrogen-14, which makes up the vast majority of naturally occurring nitrogen, andnitrogen-15. Fourteen radioactive isotopes (radioisotopes) have also been found so far, with atomic masses ranging from 10 to 25, and one nuclear isomer, 11mN.</skos:definition>
