Columbia, Canada
&quot;http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/hfd/library/documents/glossary/&quot;
New Value=From the Glossary of Forestry Terms, Ministry of Forests, Government of British
Columbia, Canada
&quot;http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/hfd/library/documents/glossary/&quot;</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-09-25 User Id=tstevens Entity=WeightedRelation Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert WeightedRelation
New Value=id: null
related concept uuid: b3a1e091-0bc2-4c9b-a89c-bd003fdd5889
relationship type: null
relationship value: null
generated by: null</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="From the Glossary of Forestry Terms, Ministry of Forests, Government of British Columbia, Canada &apos;http://www.for.gov.bc.ca/hfd/library/documents/glossary/&apos;" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Afforestation is the establishment of trees on an area that has lacked forestcover for a very long time or has never been forested. Reforestation is thenatural or artificial restocking (i.e., planting, seeding) of an area withforest trees. Also called forest regeneration.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-09-25 09:43:31.0</dcterms:modified>
