    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">ENHANCED FUJITA SCALE RATING</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2016-06-28 User Id=saritz Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: A six-level numerical, damage-based classification of estimated wind speeds. Following suspected high-wind events, affected areas are surveyed to provide an EF-scale rating. These high-wind events are typically tornadoes. However, the EF scale has also been applied to downbursts and tropical cyclones.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2016-06-28 User Id=saritz Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=ENHANCED FUJITA SCALE RATING [d866f0ba-c70a-4377-9f91-58ab402f6f8b,217725] - TORNADOES [a200e677-384a-42d6-8519-1c7735f0adb9,84177]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Glossary of Meteorology, American Meteorological Society, 2016." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">A six-level numerical, damage-based classification of estimated wind speeds. Following suspected high-wind events, affected areas are surveyed to provide an EF-scale rating. These high-wind events are typically tornadoes. However, the EF scale has also been applied to downbursts and tropical cyclones.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2016-06-28 14:04:01.0</dcterms:modified>
