    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">RECLAMATION/REVEGETATION/RESTORATION</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=reference 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=National Research Council. 1992.  Restoration of Aquatic Ecosystems: science,
technology, and public policy.	  National Academy Press.  Washington, D.C.,
1992.
New Value=National Research Council. 1992.  Restoration of Aquatic Ecosystems: science, technology, and public policy.   National Academy Press.  Washington, D.C., 1992.</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-07-11 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=UPDATE Field=text 
System Note=update Definition
Old Value=Reclamation, as used here refers, to putting a natural resource to a new
or altered use.  Restoration is the return of an ecosystem to a
close approximation of its condition prior to disturbance. Revegetation is
the planting of vegetation in an area where vegetation has been removed.
New Value=Refers to putting a natural resource to a new or altered use. Restoration is the return of an ecosystem to a close approximation of its condition prior to disturbance. Revegetation is the planting of vegetation in an area where vegetation has been removed.</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="National Research Council. 1992.  Restoration of Aquatic Ecosystems: science, technology, and public policy.   National Academy Press.  Washington, D.C., 1992." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Refers to putting a natural resource to a new or altered use. Restoration is the return of an ecosystem to a close approximation of its condition prior to disturbance. Revegetation is the planting of vegetation in an area where vegetation has been removed.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2012-07-11 10:13:13.0</dcterms:modified>
