text: Phylum Phoronida. Commonly called Horeshoe worms are hermaphroditic, marine, benthic, suspension feeding vermiform animals distringuished with a looped digestive tract and the anus is located close to the mouth. Adult Phoronida live in chitinous tube attached or burrowed in a hard substrate with lophophore, ciliated feeding structure, surrounding the mouth.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="speciesidentification.org" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Phylum Phoronida. Commonly called Horeshoe worms are hermaphroditic, marine, benthic, suspension feeding vermiform animals distringuished with a looped digestive tract and the anus is located close to the mouth. Adult Phoronida live in chitinous tube attached or burrowed in a hard substrate with lophophore, ciliated feeding structure, surrounding the mouth.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2017-03-13 14:18:14.0</dcterms:modified>
