    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">HARD OR STONY CORALS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-13 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Definition added
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Scleractinia is a subclass of class Anthozoa (Phylum Cnidarian) of water-based organisms formed by colonial polyps with hexamerous symmetry, eight and ten part symmetry is not uncommon.  Stony corals, known as hard corals or &apos;reef-building corals, are sessile marine organisms that secrete a calicum carbonate skeleton to protect it&apos;s soft body.  Polyps are individual animals with a cylindrical body crowned by an oral disc and mouth surrounded by tentacles.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="encyclopedia of life" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Scleractinia is a subclass of class Anthozoa (Phylum Cnidarian) of water-based organisms formed by colonial polyps with hexamerous symmetry, eight and ten part symmetry is not uncommon.  Stony corals, known as hard corals or &apos;reef-building corals, are sessile marine organisms that secrete a calicum carbonate skeleton to protect it&apos;s soft body.  Polyps are individual animals with a cylindrical body crowned by an oral disc and mouth surrounded by tentacles.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2017-03-13 14:09:01.0</dcterms:modified>
