    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">TILL PLAINS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-08-26 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: An extensive flat plain of glacial till that forms when a sheet of ice becomes detached from the main body of a glacier and melts in place depositing the sediments it carried. A till plain with irregular topography is referred to as a ground moraine.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-08-06 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=TILL PLAINS [bffac466-83aa-4060-a378-6d2d6e49f2a1,105637] - GLACIAL LANDFORMS [b895f4b5-5273-49ef-883f-b67d9f199505,105287]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">An extensive flat plain of glacial till that forms when a sheet of ice becomes detached from the main body of a glacier and melts in place depositing the sediments it carried. A till plain with irregular topography is referred to as a ground moraine.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-08-26 08:49:54.0</dcterms:modified>
