New Value=NORTH TROPICAL ATLANTIC INDEX [d52674c3-0c78-4f35-9675-c2a8b3869b16,21451] - SEA SURFACE TEMPERATURE INDICES [b83895e9-bac8-49fe-bcf5-8fe4d8fcaa16,39747]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Earth Systems Research Laboratory, Physical Sciences Division, NOAA, http://www.esrl.noaa.gov/psd/data/climateindices/list/#NTA  Penland, C., and L. Matrosova, 1998: &apos;Prediction of tropical Atlantic sea aurface temperatures using Linear Inverse Modeling,&apos; J. Climate, March, 483-496 pp." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The timeseries of SST anomalies averaged over 60W to 20W, 6N to 18N and 20W to 10W, 6N to 10N map. Data is obtained from the COADS dataset for 1951-1991 and NCEP afterwards. Anomalies were calculated relative to the 1951-2000 climatology, smoothed by three months running mean procedure and projected onto 20 leading EOFs. Month of data is the center of the 3 months that are smoothed. More information and the indexes forecasted values are available.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2020-02-14 13:05:30.0</dcterms:modified>
