    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">PEATLANDS</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2017-03-15 User Id=mgenazzi Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Definition added
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Peatlands are areas formed by a brown mass of organic matter in which twigs, roots, and other plant parts can still be recognized.  These areas formed due to lack of enough oxygen to decay vegetation completely on land. Peatlands form in fresh-water swamps, indicated by the plant fossils.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
