    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">HYDROGEN PRODUCTION/USE</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-29 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Refers to the production and use of hydrogen power for human consumption. Hydrogen-containing compounds such as fossil fuels, biomass or even water can be a source of hydrogen. Thermochemical processes can be used to produce hydrogen from biomass and from fossil fuels such as coal, natural gas and petroleum. Power generated from sunlight, wind and nuclear sources can be used to produce hydrogen electrolytically.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2012-06-26 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=HYDROGEN PRODUCTION/USE [c346378a-09ee-428c-89c1-c94354cdc74f,40109] - ENERGY PRODUCTION/USE [b73cee46-8e2c-4df9-b1ed-7f0aa98a04ac,40101]</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="U.S. Department of Energy" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Refers to the production and use of hydrogen power for human consumption. Hydrogen-containing compounds such as fossil fuels, biomass or even water can be a source of hydrogen. Thermochemical processes can be used to produce hydrogen from biomass and from fossil fuels such as coal, natural gas and petroleum. Power generated from sunlight, wind and nuclear sources can be used to produce hydrogen electrolytically.</skos:definition>
