  <skos:Concept rdf:about="c39bf4db-70d3-4921-bd5e-e7c390a980bb">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="d2f152e1-7398-44ad-b0a4-77ee6ef5bd6c"/>
    <dcterms:created>2024-02-28</dcterms:created>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">DNA METABARCODING</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=DNA METABARCODING [c39bf4db-70d3-4921-bd5e-e7c390a980bb,1603369] - OMICS METHODOLOGY [d2f152e1-7398-44ad-b0a4-77ee6ef5bd6c,1603367]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2024-02-28 User Id=tstevens Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: DNA metabarcoding is a developing approach that identifies multiple species from a mixed sample (bulk DNA or eDNA) based on high-throughput sequencing (HTS) of a specific DNA marker. It differs from conventional DNA barcoding (usually based on Sanger sequencing of individual specimens) because the amount of DNA sequence data derived by HTS allows taxonomy to be rapidly assigned to many species present in a sample.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://resjournals.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/een.12831#:~:text=DNA%20metabarcoding%20is%20a%20developing,of%20a%20specific%20DNA%20marker" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">DNA metabarcoding is a developing approach that identifies multiple species from a mixed sample (bulk DNA or eDNA) based on high-throughput sequencing (HTS) of a specific DNA marker. It differs from conventional DNA barcoding (usually based on Sanger sequencing of individual specimens) because the amount of DNA sequence data derived by HTS allows taxonomy to be rapidly assigned to many species present in a sample.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2024-02-28 12:17:14.0</dcterms:modified>
