System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: The major ions, sodium (Na+), calcium (Ca2+), and chloride (Cl−), deposited in central Antarctica and preserved in ice cores originate from both marine and continental sources. They provide important proxy records, helping to reconstruct past climatic processes.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2015-10-29 User Id=aaleman Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
