    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Aerosol deposited in East Antarctica over the last glacial cycle: detailed apportionment of continental and sea-salt contributions, Bigler, Matthias, Rothlisberger, Regine, Lambert, Fabrice, Stocker, Thomas F., Wagenbach, Dietmar, 1 January, 2006, Journal of Geophysical Research / 111, 14pp, 10.1029/2005JD006469" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The major ions, sodium (Na+), calcium (Ca2+), and chloride (Cl−), deposited in central Antarctica and preserved in ice cores originate from both marine and continental sources. They provide important proxy records, helping to reconstruct past climatic processes.</skos:definition>
