    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-03-05 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=BroaderRelation Operation=INSERT 
User Note=Insert Concept
System Note=add broader relation
New Value=PLUCKING [c4619d3d-f852-4899-9e33-9fd6d4096351,82805] - GLACIAL PROCESSES [d7b62912-5970-46b1-be45-6a603c9a6979,82723]</skos:changeNote>
    <skos:changeNote>Date=2013-04-01 User Id=tbs1979 Entity=Definition Operation=INSERT 
System Note=insert Definition
New Value=id: null
text: Exploits pre-existing fractures in the bedrock. This plays a key role in opening and creating new fractures but has only provided small segments of loose material. This is then followed by the entrainment of the loosened rock by the ice. During the process of entrainment, loose rock material is frozen onto the base of the glacier and incorporated into the glacial ice.
language code: en</skos:changeNote>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="PhysicalGeography.net" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Exploits pre-existing fractures in the bedrock. This plays a key role in opening and creating new fractures but has only provided small segments of loose material. This is then followed by the entrainment of the loosened rock by the ice. During the process of entrainment, loose rock material is frozen onto the base of the glacier and incorporated into the glacial ice.</skos:definition>
    <dcterms:modified>2013-04-01 11:20:15.0</dcterms:modified>
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/sciencekeywords"/>
  </skos:Concept>
  <skos:Concept rdf:about="ed7c506e-b18e-4a93-ac03-4bdfe119b72f">
    <skos:broader rdf:resource="c7b5c02c-724d-4a19-b824-98180f3900c9"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">NITROGEN</skos:prefLabel>
    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Starr, C. and R.Taggart. 1998. Biology: the unity and diversity of life. Wadsworth Publishing Company. Belmont, California." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">Nitrogen is a plant nutrient that is a component of proteins, nucleicacids, coenzymes, and chlorophylls.  Plants that are deficient in nitrogenhave stunted growth, and light-green older leaves.</skos:definition>
