    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="Adapted from: Dictionary of Earth Science, 5th ed.. 1997.  Sybil Parker, ed. in chief. McGraw-Hill." xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The degree to which an electrical current can pass through water due to ions dissolved in the water. Salinity is often calculated from conductivity and temperature.</skos:definition>
