    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/B9780128199909000123" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">In the context of genomes, assembly refers to the process of taking a large number of short DNA sequences and putting them back together to create a representation of the original chromosomes from which the DNA originated.</skos:definition>
