text: Phylum Chordata. Class Hyperoartia. Order Petromyzontiformes. Lampreys have a sucking disk for mouth, no jaw, elongates, cylindrical, flexible body distinguished by no scales covered with mucous, a rounded tail, separated dorsal fins with no spines. Phylum Chordata. Class Myxini. Hagfish as distinguished from lampreys by the prescence four  pairs of tentacles around their mouth and a skull but no vetebrae column
