    <gcmd:reference gcmd:text="NCDC:  http://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/societal-impacts/redti/" xml:lang="en"/>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">The Residential Energy Demand Temperature Index (REDTI) is based on population weighted* heating and cooling degree days, and as such, is a valuable tool for explaining year-to-year fluctuations in energy demand for residential heating and cooling. Residential energy consumption is known to be highly correlated with heating and cooling degree days.</skos:definition>
